WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:01.630
- Just to let you know that

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:03.350
the flight time's going to be roughly

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.678
a minute and twenty seconds today.

00:00:05.678 --> 00:00:08.428
(engine revving)

00:00:12.902 --> 00:00:17.095
- [Narrator] This is
Westray Island Airport.

00:00:17.095 --> 00:00:20.428
And this is Papa Westray Island Airport.

00:00:21.326 --> 00:00:24.250
They're only 1.7 miles
away from each other

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.643
and are connected by the world's
shortest commercial flight.

00:00:27.643 --> 00:00:31.310
The average flying time
is about 80 seconds.

00:00:32.305 --> 00:00:34.025
These two islands are a part of the

00:00:34.025 --> 00:00:36.546
Orkney Islands in Northern Scotland.

00:00:36.546 --> 00:00:40.307
This archipelago is defined
by jagged coastlines,

00:00:40.307 --> 00:00:43.465
and its obvious lack of trees.

00:00:43.465 --> 00:00:45.044
There are 70 islands in total,

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:47.379
only 20 of them are inhabited.

00:00:47.379 --> 00:00:49.152
On some islands, like Papa Westray,

00:00:49.152 --> 00:00:52.193
the population is less than 100.

00:00:52.193 --> 00:00:55.691
To get around up here most people fly

00:00:55.691 --> 00:00:59.608
on this plane, the
inter-island Loganair route.

00:01:02.143 --> 00:01:04.520
Colin here, he's the head pilot.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:05.858
- I'm Colin McAllister,

00:01:05.858 --> 00:01:07.721
I'm the senior pilot.

00:01:07.721 --> 00:01:11.326
The aircraft we fly in Orkney,
it carries 8 passengers.

00:01:11.326 --> 00:01:12.698
The highest that we've reached

00:01:12.698 --> 00:01:14.842
would be about 350 feet altitude.

00:01:14.842 --> 00:01:16.347
So it's quite low.

00:01:16.347 --> 00:01:19.578
It flies at around about 150 miles an hour

00:01:19.578 --> 00:01:21.707
and it has the aerodynamics of a brick,

00:01:21.707 --> 00:01:25.632
but it is super for what
we do in the islands.

00:01:25.632 --> 00:01:27.842
- [Narrator] So why
does this flight exist?

00:01:27.842 --> 00:01:30.857
Because there are so few
people in the Orkney Islands,

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:33.807
building bridges doesn't
make financial sense,

00:01:33.807 --> 00:01:36.143
they just wouldn't get enough use.

00:01:36.143 --> 00:01:37.749
So, if you live up here,

00:01:37.749 --> 00:01:40.792
there are only two ways to get around.

00:01:40.792 --> 00:01:43.533
One, you can take this ferry,

00:01:43.533 --> 00:01:45.577
which is super, super slow.

00:01:45.577 --> 00:01:47.327
Or, two, you can fly.

00:01:49.021 --> 00:01:49.997
- My name is Kate,

00:01:49.997 --> 00:01:51.609
and I live on Orkney mainland,

00:01:51.609 --> 00:01:54.020
but I fly out to several of the islands

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.350
teaching music on a weekly basis.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:57.436
Once every three weeks

00:01:57.436 --> 00:02:00.088
I'm flying the shortest
flight to get to work.

00:02:00.088 --> 00:02:03.054
- The flight is used
almost like a bus service.

00:02:03.054 --> 00:02:04.627
- [Narrator] It acts like a bus route,

00:02:04.627 --> 00:02:05.710
but it's not.

00:02:06.657 --> 00:02:08.309
It takes a team,

00:02:08.309 --> 00:02:10.180
from the two air traffic controllers,

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:12.144
- Okay, you're clear to land.

00:02:12.144 --> 00:02:13.739
- [Narrator] To the four firefighters,

00:02:13.739 --> 00:02:16.300
they all work together to
help keep the flight safe.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.604
- [Colin] Over the years I've flown

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:20.107
somewhere between four
and five thousand times

00:02:20.107 --> 00:02:22.183
between Westray and Papa Westray.

00:02:22.183 --> 00:02:24.254
It is community spirit that drives

00:02:24.254 --> 00:02:27.014
the people who work at the airfields.

00:02:27.014 --> 00:02:27.919
- [Narrator] The world's shortest flight

00:02:27.919 --> 00:02:30.104
has been around for a long time.

00:02:30.104 --> 00:02:31.759
- This year I've been flying it

00:02:31.759 --> 00:02:33.952
for 50 years in Orkney.

00:02:33.952 --> 00:02:36.978
- [Narrator] At this point
it's a well-oiled machine.

00:02:36.978 --> 00:02:38.958
Our only complaint?

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.375
No drink service.

